tests:
  unit: { count: 160, covers: "The CA's DER is the certificate its PEM carries, and a PEM with no certificate has none. The profile parses as one Configuration holding one com.apple.security.root payload whose data decodes to that DER, named Trawler Proxy CA, with UUIDs equal across builds of one CA and different for another. Reach's ca_urls name the bound API socket once per format, brackets kept for IPv6. A sweep over every platform x host x armed-or-not asserts each certificate task names exactly one of CA_FILES, its URL and save control are that format's, and every command reads that name; the iPhone gets the profile in Safari and never a .pem, Android and the emulator trawler-ca.cer, every other platform PEM, and each installer step names the file to pick. Every platform carries a not-decrypting check: the iPhone's trust switch and Safari, Android's User store and Chrome, the Simulator's restart, the desktops' browser restart, Firefox and pinning; the iPhone's trust step says installing does not trust. caFile fetches each format's path as bytes and throws on a failure; caCertPem reads /ca.pem. The walkthrough judge refuses a finding past R30." }
  integration: { count: 245, covers: "Each of /ca.crt, /ca.pem, /ca.cer and /ca.mobileconfig answers with its content type and a file name matching its URL; both PEM routes carry the CA byte for byte, /ca.cer its DER, and the profile its DER as the root payload; a CA that is not a certificate fails the two derived routes with 500. An armed core's /reach names the three URLs over the armed API address and each answers there; a fresh core names none. On the setup screen the iPhone's save control saves the profile and the emulator's the DER, each named in its note by that file, and this machine's saves the PEM under the name its steps run against. With traffic arriving undecrypted, the certificate task on the iPhone, Android and this Mac shows the refusal followed by that platform's check." }
  e2e: { waived: "The epic plan gives the journeys to W6, and no hermetic run has an iPhone or an Android device. The evidence is the owner's installs on a real iPhone (the profile from Safari, full trust on, example.com decrypted) and a real Android phone, and the walkthrough re-run through the real window: green at 3560bc0, 24 reels and 150 chapters, the device reels' armed and not-decrypting frames each showing what its caption says." }
